---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Shoichi Seto -- developer, builder, exploring the intersection of structure and nature." lang="en">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-display tracking-tight">About</h1>

    <div class="prose mt-8">
      <p>
        Shoichi Seto. Developer based in Tokyo.
      </p>

      <p>
        Ph.D. student (1st year) at the University of Tokyo, Dept. of Aeronautics
        and Astronautics, Nakasuka-Funase-Ikari Lab. Building
        <a href="https://syntopic.io">SynTopic</a>, a knowledge structuring platform
        spun out of research on knowledge engineering and model-based development
        for satellite systems.
      </p>

      <h2>Timeline</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>2019 Apr -- Entered the University of Tokyo. Joined RoboTech (robotics club), responsible for software/control. Competed at world championship.</li>
        <li>2021 Apr -- Entered Dept. of Aeronautics and Astronautics. Joined Matsuo Lab AI team. Won 2nd place at WRC 2020 AI robot competition.</li>
        <li>2021 Nov -- Developed the world's first drone-type CanSat. Won 1st place in Japan. PM and software lead.</li>
        <li>2022 Apr -- Entered Graduate School of Engineering, Dept. of Aeronautics and Astronautics. Nakasuka-Funase Lab. Led satellite software development for CubeSat missions.</li>
        <li>2023 Apr -- Started research project on knowledge structuring and model-based development, drawing on satellite development experience and knowledge engineering research.</li>
        <li>2025 Aug -- Founded SynTopic Inc. as a University of Tokyo startup, to bring the research outcomes to production.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Interests</h2>

      <p>
        Structured knowledge, distributed systems, and the quiet patterns
        of the natural world. Coffee, music, travel, and Shih Tzu dogs.
      </p>

      <h2>This site</h2>

      <p>
        Built with Astro 6, Tailwind CSS v4, and TypeScript.
        Dark mode default (cosmic theme), warm color palette
        inspired by coffee and earth tones.
        Source on <a href="https://github.com/flap1/about">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
